<title>USA: UPS chairman says Teamsters, UPS &quot;closer&quot;.</title>
<headline>UPS chairman says Teamsters, UPS &quot;closer&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Parcel Service Chairman James Kelly said on Monday the company and the Teamsters union were closer to a settlement to the two-week-old strike than they were four days ago.</p>
<p>But he predicted that the strike could continue for &quot;much, much longer&quot; if talks broke off this week.</p>
